---
import WritingLayout from '../../layouts/WritingLayout.astro';
import ChloeArchitecture from '../../components/ChloeArchitecture.astro';
const decisions = [
  { title: 'Match both meaning and exact names', text: 'Students may describe a program differently from the website, but exact names still matter. I combined semantic search, using Titan Text Embeddings v2, with BM25 keyword search in Weaviate. This supports both kinds of questions, though the results still depend on what has been indexed and how current it is.' },
  { title: 'Search the knowledge base first', text: 'The agent starts with the curated knowledge base. If that does not answer the question, it can search official FSU sites through Exa. I limited each exchange to two knowledge-base searches and one web search to keep the search scope and usage under control.' },
  { title: 'Stream answers from a serverless API', text: 'I hosted FastAPI on AWS Lambda through the Lambda Web Adapter, so there is no continuously running application server to manage. The interface shows text as it arrives, then replaces the draft with the final answer and checked source list. The tradeoffs are startup delays and the possibility that draft text changes after the source check.' },
];
---
<WritingLayout title="Chloe: a RAG assistant for CCI, FSU">
  <article>
    <p class="kicker">Architecture Case Study</p>
    <p class="lead">I built Chloe to help students and visitors find answers about programs, admissions, and funding at Florida State University’s College of Communication &amp; Information (CCI). It searches official college and university content, links factual answers to their sources, and asks a follow-up question when it needs more detail.</p>
    <dl class="project-facts">
      <div><dt>Scope</dt><dd>Content preparation → search → chat</dd></div>
      <div><dt>Core stack</dt><dd>FastAPI · Bedrock · Weaviate · AWS Lambda</dd></div>
    </dl>
    <section aria-labelledby="problem-title">
      <h2 id="problem-title">The problem</h2>
      <p>CCI has three schools, and the right answer can depend on the school, program, or student level. A question such as “When is the application deadline?” needs more context before the assistant can give a useful answer.</p>
      <p>I wanted visitors to get a clear answer and a page they could check for themselves. The design also needed to handle unclear questions, acknowledge missing information, and keep the cost of each exchange under control.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="solution-title">
      <h2 id="solution-title">The solution</h2>
      <p>Chloe uses retrieval-augmented generation (RAG): it looks up relevant content and gives that information to the model to help it answer. An AI agent decides when to search, when to ask for clarification, and when a question falls outside its scope.</p>
      <p>The system has three parts: a pipeline that prepares the knowledge base, a FastAPI service that runs the agent, and a chat interface that displays the answer as it arrives. The agent uses Claude Haiku 4.5 through Amazon Bedrock, coordinated by pydantic-ai.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="ingestion-title">
      <h2 id="ingestion-title">Preparing the knowledge base</h2>
      <p>The pipeline starts with a curated list of pages fetched through Firecrawl. It removes repeated website content and breaks each page into smaller sections using its headings. Each section keeps a link back to its source, while FAQs and reference pages receive their own treatment.</p>
      <p>Before indexing, Claude Haiku adds a short description to help place each section in context. Titan v2 then converts the text into a numerical representation for search. The pipeline skips unchanged documents and, during full runs, removes content no longer on the source list. That avoids unnecessary processing, but the list still needs to be maintained.</p>
    </section>
    <ChloeArchitecture />
    <section aria-labelledby="decisions-title">
      <h2 id="decisions-title">Architecture decisions</h2>
      <div class="decisions">{decisions.map(decision => <div class="decision"><h3>{decision.title}</h3><p>{decision.text}</p></div>)}</div>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="controls-title">
      <h2 id="controls-title">Keeping answers grounded and usage bounded</h2>
      <p>Cloudflare Turnstile checks requests before they reach paid model or search services. The agent receives only the last six conversation turns as quoted context. Each question allows up to <strong>five tool calls</strong> and <strong>eight model requests</strong>, with a <strong>60-second</strong> execution limit and an <strong>800-token</strong> limit per model response.</p>
      <p>Before sending the final factual answer, the backend removes source links that were not returned by a search. If none remain, Chloe says it could not find a reliable answer. This checks where the links came from; it does not prove every claim is correct. Broader traffic limits, spending controls, and protection against malicious instructions remain separate concerns.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="operations-title">
      <h2 id="operations-title">Deploying and monitoring the service</h2>
      <p>I used Terraform to define the AWS infrastructure and encrypted Systems Manager parameters to supply secrets at startup. CloudWatch captures application logs. Langfuse traces model and search activity through OpenTelemetry, making it possible to inspect individual exchanges and token usage.</p>
      <p>Running the service also means monitoring its dependencies: Bedrock, Weaviate, external search, and access to the required secrets.</p>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="demonstration-title">
      <h2 id="demonstration-title">Leadership Board demonstration</h2>
      <p>I presented the assistant at a CCI Leadership Board meeting at Florida State University. Attendees tried it live with questions about the college, alongside off-topic and playful prompts. In those interactions, the assistant stayed within its intended scope.</p>
      <p>Seeing people try their own questions gave me feedback beyond prepared examples and a chance to discuss the design with college leadership.</p>
      <a class="recap-link" href="https://lnkd.in/p/eJTJ_A8f" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer">Read the presentation recap ↗</a>
    </section>
    <section aria-labelledby="outcome-title">
      <h2 id="outcome-title">Results and lessons</h2>
      <p>In a small initial evaluation, <strong>88% of factual responses were graded correct</strong> by an AI judge against the retrieved source text. This is an early indication of answer quality, with human review still needed.</p>
      <p>The results suggest Chloe handles straightforward factual questions more reliably than ambiguous ones. Asking for clarification before searching and handling failed requests more gracefully are the main areas to improve.</p>
      <p>The current estimated cost is <strong>about $0.01 per question-and-answer exchange</strong>. Broader evaluation, response-time measurement, and simultaneous-user testing are next steps.</p>
    </section>
    <a class="closing-link" href="/#projects">← Explore other projects</a>
  </article>
</WritingLayout>
<style>
  article { margin-top:24px; }
  .kicker { color:var(--orange);font:12px/1.6 var(--font-mono); }
  .lead { max-width:66ch;font-size:clamp(18px,2vw,21px);line-height:1.65;color:var(--muted);margin:20px 0 32px; }
  .project-facts { display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr 1.4fr;gap:24px;margin:0;padding:20px 0;border-block:1px solid var(--line); }
  dt { font:11px/1.6 var(--font-mono);color:var(--orange);margin-bottom:6px; }
  dd { margin:0;font-size:14px;line-height:1.6; }
  section { margin-block:48px;max-width:72ch; }
  h2 { font-size:clamp(24px,3vw,30px);line-height:1.2;letter-spacing:-.025em;margin:0 0 18px; }
  section > h2::after { content:'';display:block;width:72px;height:2px;background:var(--orange);margin-top:14px; }
  h3 { font-size:19px;line-height:1.4;letter-spacing:-.015em;margin:0 0 10px; }
  p { color:var(--muted);font-size:16px;line-height:1.8; }
  .decision + .decision { margin-top:24px;padding-top:24px;border-top:1px solid var(--line); }
  .decision p { margin-bottom:0; }
  strong { color:var(--ink);font-weight:500;text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:color-mix(in srgb,var(--orange) 55%,transparent);text-underline-offset:4px;text-decoration-thickness:1px; }
  section[aria-labelledby="outcome-title"] { padding:24px;border-left:2px solid var(--orange);background:color-mix(in srgb,var(--orange) 4%,var(--bg)); }
  section[aria-labelledby="outcome-title"] > h2::after { display:none; }
  section[aria-labelledby="outcome-title"] p:last-child { margin-bottom:0; }
  .recap-link { display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;color:var(--ink);text-decoration:underline;text-decoration-color:var(--orange);text-underline-offset:5px;transition:color 160ms; }
  .recap-link:hover { color:var(--orange); }
  .closing-link { display:inline-flex;align-items:center;min-height:44px;color:var(--muted);border-bottom:1px solid var(--line);transition:color 160ms; }
  .closing-link:hover { color:var(--ink); }
  @media(max-width:639px) { .project-facts { grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:16px; }section { margin-block:36px; } }
</style>
